{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require social care workers to undergo dysphagia training",
        "additional_details": "Dysphagia (swallowing difficulty) affects 1 in 5 elderly adults, yet awareness training for care staff remains non-mandatory, leaving lives at risk daily. We call on the UK government to make dysphagia training compulsory for all care staff, including symptom recognition, emergency response, and care plan updates. This knowledge can prevent choking.",
        "background": "To make dysphagia awareness a mandatory training requirement for workers in care settings for those with Learning Disabilities and vulnerable adults.",
